# There is nothing to configure. That is not a placeholder — it is the design.
#
# The Sand Pavilion runs completely with no environment file at all: the Library
# reads from the bundled src/game/data/seed.js, everything you add lives on your
# own machine, and the app makes zero network requests. There is no account, no
# key, and no service to sign up for.
#
# This file used to hold Supabase credentials. The hosted backend was DELETED
# outright on 2026-08-02 rather than left dormant — see CLAUDE.md's 2026-07-12
# standing decision and plans/SELF-HOSTED-STACK-PLAN.md for where the backend
# is actually going (local Postgres + local MinIO, in Docker, on your machine).
#
# The file is kept, empty, so that the moment something genuinely optional does
# appear there is an obvious place for it — and so anyone looking can see at a
# glance that the answer today is "nothing".
#
# One rule that outlives any particular variable: a SERVICE_ROLE-class key, or
# any other secret, never belongs in a file that git can see. Set it as an
# environment variable in the one terminal session that needs it.
